  <prompt>
    Add a NEW read-only, stateless `POST /api/compose/project` endpoint that takes docx bytes and returns a
    `ComposeServerProjection` — NO persistence, NO authoring — so browse-local `.docx` renders via the SERVER
    reader instead of the lossy client `mammoth` fallback. Update the client browse effect (`ComposeWorkspace.tsx`)
    to send the browsed bytes to this endpoint and hydrate `projection`. This is FR-03 and resolves ADR Tension
    T-2: it does NOT violate ADR-040 / R4 I-2 — the client authors nothing; the server only READS. Document that
    explicitly in the PR. The alternative (a client-side projection path) is rejected because it re-introduces a
    second reader and breaks F-2 (single auditable reader).
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (BFF + Compose client). Expert in the R4 server projection, the ADR-040 browse-client-only boundary, and the `byte[]`-in/projection-out contract. Follow ADRs strictly and surface tensions per §6.5.</role>

  <goal>
    A new stateless `POST /api/compose/project` endpoint (bytes → `ComposeServerProjection`, no persistence, no
    authoring) exists; the client browse effect sends browsed bytes and hydrates `projection`; browse-local `.docx`
    renders via the server projection branch (no `mammoth`). The PR documents T-2 as a resolved path-A exception.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Browse-local docs are client-only by design (ADR-040 — no BFF round-trip for authoring). Today that means
      browsed `.docx` falls back to the lossy client `mammoth` reader, breaking F-2 (single reader) and legal
      read-fidelity. WS-1 routes browse through the SAME server reader via a read-only, stateless projection
      round-trip. Because the server only reads (returns a projection, persists nothing, authors nothing), the
      "client never authors bytes" invariant (I-2) is preserved — this is the design-time resolution of Tension
      T-2 (design §9, spec T-2). `POST /api/compose/upload` exists but PERSISTS, so it cannot be reused for browse.
      Line numbers are indicative — RE-GREP before editing.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs — add the new `POST /api/compose/project` route (stateless, no-persist)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs / IComposeService.cs — add a stateless project-from-bytes method reusing `ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder`</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs — the single reader to reuse; returns the Load-path projection shape</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/IComposeService.cs:356-362 — the projection shape `project` must also return</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx — browse client effect sends bytes to `project` and hydrates `projection`</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/seam/ — seam slice for the browse→project (no-persist) path (ADR-038)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">Upload path returns a projection — establishes the projection-hydration client pattern and the reusable server projection call this task mirrors (no-persist variant).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-03">The `project` endpoint MUST be read-only and stateless — bytes → projection, NO persistence, NO authoring. Scope: it MUST NOT write to the session ledger, SPE, or any store; a call leaves zero server-side state.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-040 / R4 I-2">The client MUST author no bytes; browse stays client-only for authoring. Scope: sending browsed bytes to a read-only server reader is a projection round-trip, NOT authoring — document this as the T-2 path-A resolution in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">`byte[]`-in / projection-out; no `Microsoft.Graph` above `SpeFileStore`. Scope: `project` reads bytes via `ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder` entirely inside `Services/Compose/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">No AI-internal type injected into the `project` path; `Services/Compose/` stays pure (Tier-1 NetArchTest). Scope: consume `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` seams only if ever needed — not needed here.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Add a seam slice for the browse→project vertical slice at its KEEP path, asserting the projection matches the Load-path shape AND that nothing is persisted. Scope: no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`/DI-registration/ctor-null tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / BFF Hygiene §10">State the Placement Justification in the PR (cite `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`); measure compressed publish size, report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB (expected ~0 MB). Scope: run `/conflict-check` before the PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Stateless read-only projection endpoint; ADR-040 browse boundary; T-2 path-A resolution; BFF hygiene + seam testing</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
