    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Upload projection wiring (persisting)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs">
        Task 010's upload→projection wiring is the template; `project` is the no-persist sibling (drop the persistence, keep the projection build).
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Single docx→projection reader" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs">
        The one reader `project` reuses so browse renders through the same auditable code path (F-2).
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the FULL rigor-level declaration. Load spec FR-03 + Tension T-2, design §4/§9, ADR-040/007/013/038, `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Re-grep the anchors">RE-GREP the upload endpoint (010's wiring), the Load-path projection shape (`IComposeService.cs:356-362`), and the browse client effect in `ComposeWorkspace.tsx`. Confirm where browse currently falls back to `mammoth`.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Add the stateless project method (server)">Add a stateless `project(bytes) → ComposeServerProjection` method to `ComposeService.cs`/`IComposeService.cs` reusing `ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder`; persist NOTHING (no ledger, no SPE). Add `POST /api/compose/project` in `ComposeEndpoints.cs` returning the Load-path projection shape.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Checkpoint">Run `context-handoff` (silent: "✅ Checkpoint.").</step>
    <step order="4" name="Wire the browse effect (client)">Update the browse effect in `ComposeWorkspace.tsx` to POST browsed bytes to `project` and hydrate `projection`, so browse takes the projection branch — no `mammoth`.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Seam slice">Add a seam slice asserting browse→project returns the Load-path projection shape AND persists nothing (ADR-038).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Build + hygiene + PR justification">Build BFF + client; run suite + seam. Publish-size report (delta vs ~49.63 MB, ~0 expected). Run `/conflict-check`. Write the PR Placement Justification AND the T-2 path-A note (server reads only; client authors nothing).</step>
    <step order="7" name="Set task ✅ in tasks/TASK-INDEX.md">Update `projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set task 011 status to ✅. Record any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If code-review reads the browse round-trip as byte-authoring (an ADR-040 / I-2 concern) rather than a read-only projection — do NOT proceed silently. Surface it as the T-2 documented exception per root CLAUDE.md §6.5 (ADR Conflict — Resolution Required), citing the design-time path-A resolution.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>`POST /api/compose/upload` exists (`ComposeEndpoints.cs:913-920`) but PERSISTS the uploaded doc; no stateless read-only projection route exists. Verified by grepping `ComposeEndpoints.cs` for `MapPost`/`compose/` routes.</existing>
    <extension>No — browse is client-only per ADR-040 and must not persist; the upload endpoint's persistence makes it the wrong tool. A distinct stateless, no-persist read-only projection endpoint is required. It reuses the existing `ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder` reader (no new reader), so only the route/persistence boundary is new.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it, browse-local `.docx` keeps falling back to the lossy `mammoth` reader — breaking F-2 (single auditable reader) and legal read-fidelity (wrong numbering, dropped glyphs, lost alignment) on the browse entry path.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs (new `POST /api/compose/project`)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs / IComposeService.cs (stateless project-from-bytes)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx (browse effect uses `project`)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/ (browse→project no-persist seam slice)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given docx bytes POSTed to `/api/compose/project`, when the request completes, then the response is a `ComposeServerProjection` of the Load-path shape (`IComposeService.cs:356-362`) and NOTHING is persisted (no ledger/SPE write).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a browse-local `.docx`, when the browse effect runs, then it POSTs the bytes to `project`, hydrates `projection`, and the editor takes the projection branch — NOT `mammoth`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a second `project` call for the same bytes leaves zero cumulative server-side state (idempotent, stateless) — the endpoint never authors or stores bytes (ADR-040 / I-2 preserved).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the `project` path injects no AI-internal type and reaches no `Microsoft.Graph` above `SpeFileStore` — Tier-1 NetArchTest green (ADR-007/013).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A seam slice asserts the browse→project shape AND no-persistence; no banned mock/DI/ctor test added (ADR-038).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR documents T-2 as a resolved path-A exception (server reads only; client authors nothing) and states the Placement Justification; publish delta ~0 MB (≤60 MB); `/conflict-check` clean.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">TASK-INDEX.md shows task 011 as ✅ and any deviation is recorded in projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/notes/.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Spec FR-03 + Tension T-2; design §4 WS-1 + §9. The endpoint is read-only by contract — reviewers should verify
    the no-persist invariant, not just the shape. Numbering is still not fixed here (WS-3); browse gains the same
    R4 projection wins as upload (alignment/tabs/comments).
  </notes>

